Two configs:

  screenshots-ready.json   Only captures verified against the current build.
                           SAFE TO SHIP. Renders to docs/appstore-ready/
  screenshots.json         Full four-slide set including the 30 W spotlight.
                           BLOCKED until port-c3-30w.png is recaptured.

    swift Tools/makeshots.swift screenshots-ready.json
    swift Tools/makeshots.swift                          # full set

Output is gitignored — it is build output. The generator is published
standalone at github.com/bluehawana/appstore-screenshot-forapps

CAPTURE STATUS
  cable-no-emarker-60w.png   current build, correct
  port-c1-140w.png           current build, correct
  port-c2-100w.png           current build, correct
  port-c3-30w.png            STALE. Captured 20:56, three minutes before the
                             20:59 fix. Shows "Your cable is holding you back"
                             on a 30 W / 12 V port, which is the port, not the
                             cable — the exact bug that fix corrected.

TO UNBLOCK THE FOURTH SLIDE
  1. Plug the cable into the charger's 30 W port (C3 on a Nexode 200 W)
  2. Make sure the running app is the current build
  3. Cmd-Shift-4, then Space, then click the Smart Charging window
  4. Save over docs/images/port-c3-30w.png
  5. swift Tools/makeshots.swift

  It should read "Only 30 W is reaching your Mac ... this is the slow port."
  Re-running the generator without step 4 changes nothing: it composites the
  PNGs already on disk, it does not take screenshots.
